# STILL FAILS, and the server is the one at fault: the watcher learns
# the new HIGHESTMODSEQ and flag set but never gets the per-message
# FETCH updates RFC3501 2.3.2 asks for. flags.silent suppresses them
# for the session doing the store, not for anyone else. The position
# of the three FETCH lines below is a guess.
#
# the two $Label flags are new to the mailbox, so storing them makes
# the server re-announce FLAGS and PERMANENTFLAGS even though the
# store itself is silent.
depends 2180base
use watcher
send 1
10.7b enable condstore
receive 2
* ENABLED CONDSTORE
10.7b OK done
use main
send 1
10.7 store 1,3:4 +flags.silent (\Answered \Flagged \Seen \Draft $Label4 $Label5)
receive 3
* FLAGS ($Label4 $Label5 \Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS ($Label4 $Label5 \Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen \*)] permanent flags
10.7 OK done
use watcher
send 1
10.7c noop
# the flag updates were sent as soon as main made them, so they come
# before the flag list this noop announces.
receive 7
* OK [HIGHESTMODSEQ 6] next modseq - 1
* 1 FETCH (UID 1 FLAGS ($Label4 $Label5 \Answered \Draft \Flagged \Seen) MODSEQ (6))
* 3 FETCH (UID 3 FLAGS ($Label4 $Label5 \Answered \Draft \Flagged \Seen) MODSEQ (6))
* 4 FETCH (UID 4 FLAGS ($Label4 $Label5 \Answered \Draft \Flagged \Seen) MODSEQ (6))
* FLAGS ($Label4 $Label5 \Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS ($Label4 $Label5 \Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen \*)] permanent flags
10.7c OK done
end
